  "semantics": {
    "mode": "RM PDF49-50: MODE0 crystal requires OSC32_IN/OUT analog; MODE1 bypass requires OSC32_IN digital input and permits output pad GPIO. Both modes <=1MHz; retained bounds restrict nominal to32768Hz.",
    "enable_lock": "CR1 PDF69 LSEEN bit4 POR-only reset; LSELOCK bit5 prevents clearing LSEEN. It is not an oscillator-parameter lock. Configure before start, never retune while enabled.",
    "mandatory_ccs": "Own CR1 table PDF69 requires CLKCCS/HSECCS/LSECCS written1; KEY=0x5A5A. Specific table governs despite generic detector narrative describing disabled monitors.",
    "failure": "PDF57-58: startup windows1/1/1/2 seconds count256/1024/4096/16384 LSE edges. Running detector requires software-enabled unchanged LSI;128 LSE edges/256 LSI cycles. STABLE is not frequency measurement. SYSCLK fallback toHSI does not establish RTC fallback or elapsed-time continuity.",
    "gpio": "Own GPIO PDF149-151: DIR+0, SPEED+8, ANALOG+28. Oscillator pads come from current own datasheet, not the SDK recipe. Retained GPIO locks/AF and exact direct LSE_OUT routes are inspected.",
    "gate_reset": "Own SYSCTRL PDF80-85: GPIOB/C/F AHBEN+0x30 bits5/6/9 and AHBRST+0x40 same bits; RTC/UART2/UART3 APBEN1+0x38 bits3/7/8 APBRST1+0x48; AWT/UART1 APBEN2+0x34 bits13/9 APBRST2+0x44. Gate active-high, reset active-low. Configuration gate never proves working clock idle.",
    "consumers": "AWT SRC3 irrespectiveEN; UART1/2/3 SOURCE2; MCO SOURCE6; PB12AF3/PF1AF1 regardless pad enable; RTC pristine full snapshot regardlessSOURCE due independent compensation. Never reset, clear flags or rewrite retained consumers."
  },
